WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.230
I'd like to ask you something.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:11.090
Is every male college student in Japan

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:15.320
a skilled enough cook to 
make homemade pudding?

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.350
Hiromi taught me.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.080
I made this to thank you for the other day.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.200
It's so smooth...

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.220
Excellent.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:38.470
All right!

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:42.480
I'm well aware that I may be
 overstepping in saying so,

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:46.850
but why not show off this skill of yours
 to your potential girlfriend?

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.290
Mind your own business.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:54.050
I also made milk jelly, 
but I guess I should take it home.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:55.400
Why didn't you say so sooner?

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.580
I thought I was supposed 
to show off to Tanimoto-san.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.330
I never said I didn't want to eat it.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.960
Got it. Would you like it now, then?

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:09.610
If you don't mind.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:44.010
<u>Episode 6</u>
<b>Perilous Turquoise</b>

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:54.940
<b>Civil Service Lecture</b>

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.280
Preparing for the civil service exam, huh?

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:54.940
Nakata, you free?

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:57.690
Yeah. What's up, Shimomura?

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:00.240
I really need to talk to you about something.

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:04.200
This is Okita Ayumi-san. 
We're in the same club.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.660
When I told her you work at a jeweler's...

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:11.000
Please! I lost someone 
very important to me...

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:14.880
We want you to help us look for him.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:16.770
Please. I'm begging you, Nakata.

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:18.380
H-Huh?

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:21.130
It's okay now, Ayumi-chan.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.140
So that's how it is...

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:29.640
Welcome to Étranger.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:33.100
I'm the owner, Richard.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:36.600
Have a seat.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.070
Thank you.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:42.830
I heard you had a question about a gemstone.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:45.330
Yes, that's right.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:47.120
I'd like you to have a look at this.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:56.510
My boyfriend gave me this,

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:59.260
and then he suddenly went missing.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:05.010
If I may...

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:11.440
I want to know if there's a store 
selling this same accessory.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:13.850
Do you have the box?

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:15.370
No.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:18.480
Without a box from the store,
 there's nothing we can do.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.690
I don't have the box, 
but he said it was real.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:24.700
Well, is there anything else 
that might serve as a clue?

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.400
That was all he gave me.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.160
Oh, but I have his photo.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.050
His name is Furuta Yoshio.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:36.480
He works in IT.

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:38.980
He asked me to marry him.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:45.730
I think there's probably some 
reason he can't contact me...

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:53.610
But if he's really serious, I doubt 
he'd disappear without saying anything.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:57.140
If he weren't, he wouldn't 
have given me a gemstone.

00:04:57.140 --> 00:04:58.690
That's true...

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:05.720
Okita-sama, has Furuta-sama ever asked 
you to look at an accessory he designed?

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:08.340
Yes. How did you know?

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:11.580
Did you purchase said accessory?

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:16.040
No. As a student, I couldn't afford it.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:18.730
I see.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:25.590
Turquoise expresses the sender's wish 
for the recipient's happiness.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:29.530
The recipient? You mean me?

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:30.610
Yes.

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:36.100
If Furuta-sama truly wished for 
you to be happy before he left,

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:41.610
is that not a distinctly 
beautiful kind of love?

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:57.410
Nakata-kun, thank you so much.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.220
Um...

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:01.810
I'd like to thank Richard-san.

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:03.840
What does he like?

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.060
Huh?

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:09.590
Oh, I just work here part-time. I don't know.

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:10.980
Oh...

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:12.600
Well, see you.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:20.350
Shimomura, you can rest easy.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:28.760
What is it?

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:33.580
I'm hesitant to discuss it with you.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.650
Discuss what?

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:39.080
Look at this.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:42.810
What? Is this the same accessory Okita-san had?

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:47.050
Does this mean... 
you know her missing boyfriend?

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:51.000
Don't be stupid. Try polishing it.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:55.160
Will it turn into a dove or something?

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:00.920
It came off! The color came off!

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:04.090
It was probably colored using a felt-tip pen.

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:06.000
This is a false turquoise.

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:08.570
Is that common in Turkey?

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:09.840
Turkey?

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:12.860
Oh, don't get the wrong idea.

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:15.330
Turquoise isn't from Turkey.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:19.530
Currently, most turquoise 
in circulation is from America.

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:22.080
What? Then why is it called turquoise?

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.750
Because it first entered
 Europe through Turkey,

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:27.590
the French called it "turquois."

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.110
That became the English "Turkeis,"

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:34.000
signifying its origin from Turkey—

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:37.220
the namesake of both the stone and its color.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:42.900
Howlite is a gemstone with a luster 
very similar to turquoise.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:49.900
Colored howlite is commonly 
sold as "imitation turquoise."

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:52.680
Which isn't a problem if 
everyone knows that's what it is,

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:55.160
but this is different.

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:58.250
Why do you have that?

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:01.230
I borrowed it from a colleague.

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:06.840
According to him, a group of scam 
artists pretending to be jewelers

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:10.270
is systematically preying on young people.

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:11.930
Scam artists?

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:16.430
Yes. Are you familiar with date fraud?

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:19.620
Oh, yeah. Like when a guy follows 
a pretty girl to a shady place

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:24.270
and gets talked into buying a case of water 
at a thousand yen per bottle, right?

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.570
Yes.

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:30.100
It's the use of romantic feelings
 to sell expensive products.

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:33.480
Apparently, these people make money selling

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:36.950
other worthless fakes 
in addition to turquoise.

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:40.580
Like the accessory Okita-san 
said she couldn't afford!

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.110
Good for you.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:48.830
I never imagined I'd have the opportunity 
to see one of these fakes so soon.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.840
That's unforgivable.

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:55.010
Where is this group of con artists now?

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:58.040
They move around shuttered streets.

00:08:58.040 --> 00:09:01.120
Even if their neighbors complain
 and they get kicked out,

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:05.010
they simply reopen their business elsewhere.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:08.360
Really? Did you hear that 
from your colleague, too?

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:10.610
No, I looked into it.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:13.670
Looked into it? You did?

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:17.520
Do you know who they are?

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:20.420
If I did, I wouldn't be telling you.

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:22.450
Why are you mad?

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:25.960
I'm not mad.

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:32.750
Well, whatever. This kind 
of scam happens all the time.

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:42.140
It certainly does. But while this may seem 
inconsequential, they've gone too far.

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:49.550
We have a client coming. 
Please prepare for their arrival.

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:02.370
I couldn't forgive someone who 
uses gemstones to commit fraud.

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:08.120
Yeah, but I have a feeling that's not 
the only thing Richard was mad about.

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:12.670
That's why I specifically 
said it's a common scam.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:13.630
Specifically?

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:17.630
Yeah. Then Richard smiled.

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:23.720
I've never seen him like that before.

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:28.020
Seigi-kun, you must really like Richard-san.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:29.230
Huh?

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:31.770
You keep talking about him today.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:37.490
B-But I like...

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:39.450
You like what?

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.690
This chocolate tart is delicious, isn't it?

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:51.120
I found them.

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:53.380
The scam artists?

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:56.150
Yes. This is them.

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:57.190
<b>Happy Étoile</b>

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:59.630
<b>Brings good fortune! Clear the fog of past lives!</b>

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:59.630
Happy Étoile...

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:03.140
<b>It brought me
happiness</b>

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:03.140
<b>All my wishes keep coming true!!</b>

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:03.140
Is there something
 worrying <b>you</b>?

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:04.270
What's all this about?

00:11:04.270 --> 00:11:07.430
"Brings good fortune"?
"Clear the fog of past lives"?

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:11.230
It seems there are many reasons 
to disapprove of them.

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:13.400
They're into fortune-telling scams, too?

00:11:20.590 --> 00:11:22.580
Okita-san's boyfriend...

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:26.870
His real name isn't Furuta Yoshio, 
but Sasaki Yoshitsuna.

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:31.150
So they're not just selling fakes.
He's using a fake name, too.

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:35.630
By the way, Seigi, 
I noticed something interesting.

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:42.030
Tomorrow is a Sunday, but we don't 
have a single appointment scheduled.

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:44.640
You're not going to raid 
their business, are you?

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:49.010
Raid? I'm not familiar with the term.

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:52.060
It's when you barge in 
somewhere and start a fight.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:52.940
I see.

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:55.480
Are you serious?

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:59.250
No, I've never raided anyone before.

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:02.450
Seigi, do you have any acting experience?

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:05.190
Me? Of course not.

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:06.700
Do you?

00:12:07.010 --> 00:12:09.450
Well, I <i>am</i> from the land of Shakespeare.

00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:12.250
Shakespeare...

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:15.460
It wouldn't be wise to 
directly confront evildoers

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:18.890
who deceive law-abiding consumers.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:23.130
But I do think they could use 
a taste of their own medicine.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:26.280
Gotcha.

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:33.250
I had to remake it a bunch 
of times. It was tough.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:34.750
Wow, really?

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:36.400
But I think it turned out pretty well.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:38.520
Great. I can't wait.

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:48.810
This is your last chance to turn back.

00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:50.370
Don't you need a translator?

00:12:51.090 --> 00:12:51.870
Let's go.

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:06.590
Welco...

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:10.970
[I'd like to see your gemstones.]

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:12.430
What?

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:14.970
I'm sorry for the sudden intrusion.

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:18.560
This is the miracle worker who 
can sense the aura of gemstones

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:21.860
and evaluate their luck 
to bring people happiness,

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:24.110
Edward Baxter-sensei.

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:26.700
Edward Baxter?

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.290
When he passed by your shop,

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:33.550
he said he detected 
some very powerful auras,

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:35.880
so we couldn't help dropping in.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:38.710
Might we have a look at the goods?

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:41.140
Goods?

00:13:41.140 --> 00:13:44.980
Your gemstones. 
He'd like to see your gemstones.

00:13:44.980 --> 00:13:47.130
Our gemstones?

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:50.220
Thank you.

00:13:52.110 --> 00:13:53.910
One moment, please.

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:10.450
These are our gemstones.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:12.720
And what type of stone are they?

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:14.380
They're turquoises.

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:18.650
All of our gemstones possess 
auras of good fortune,

00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:21.700
with a brilliance that brings 
about a rich future.

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:24.480
Sensei, what do you think?

00:14:27.730 --> 00:14:28.840
They're cursed.

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:30.260
What? Japanese?

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:33.110
All of these gemstones are cursed.

00:14:33.110 --> 00:14:36.530
Just looking at them is dreadful.

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:37.710
Huh? What?

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:39.430
I do beg your pardon.

00:14:39.430 --> 00:14:43.440
This is the miracle worker who 
can sense the aura of gemstones

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:46.890
and evaluate their luck 
to bring people happiness,

00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:49.770
Edward Baxter-sensei.

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:53.060
Since your store is called Happy Étoile,

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:57.530
I thought we could discuss gemstones 
that bring happiness.

00:14:57.530 --> 00:14:59.160
But I can hardly believe this.

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:03.270
These gemstones bear curses 
and not an ounce of good fortune.

00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:08.170
Sensei, are you all right?

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:10.680
Their auras are affecting me.

00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:12.430
Um...

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:14.590
Show me your other gemstones.

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:15.850
Y-Yes, sir.

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:24.350
If you're here to interfere with 
our business, you can leave.

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:26.070
Otherwise, you're in for a bad time.

00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:31.570
Are you saying there's 
something worse than this store?

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:33.070
Why, you...

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:35.580
Take these turquoises.

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:38.080
Normally, these charming gemstones

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:42.420
are said to bring happiness 
to those who receive them.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:48.070
However, I can't sense a shred 
of good will from these

00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:50.340
and their mass-produced auras.

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:52.780
Keep making false accusations and...

00:15:54.380 --> 00:15:57.890
It's not the recipient 
who experiences misfortune.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:59.270
It's the sender.

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:01.270
What? The sender?

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:02.520
Yes.

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:05.350
What would happen if you sold gemstones

00:16:05.350 --> 00:16:08.940
with the intention of deceiving 
someone or out of greed?

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:13.780
The gemstones would never forgive 
those who defile them.

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:15.420
Don't be ridiculous.

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:16.940
He who hurts another...

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:18.870
...hurts himself, Sensei.

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.780
That's right.

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:24.380
Every one of these gemstones 
is surrounded by a black aura.

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:26.130
How truly miserable.

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:30.380
They don't even know how their wrongdoing 
spreads as they pass from person to person.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:32.760
If you keep talking...

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:35.510
Sasaki-sama over there is 
the perfect example.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:36.570
Huh?

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:40.380
The aura I sense from him is unique.

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:45.430
Perhaps he gave countless women 
counterfeit gemstones,

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:48.680
but there is a powerful 
grudge hanging over him.

00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:49.850
What?

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:51.110
H-He's wrong!

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:55.580
I don't sense any of that coming from you,

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:58.060
so you must have only met recently,

00:16:58.060 --> 00:17:02.410
or perhaps you don't seek a close 
relationship with each other.

00:17:02.690 --> 00:17:05.110
Hey, Miki-chan! Wait!

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:11.500
Listen, you—

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:15.370
The aura I sense around you
 is not nearly as evil.

00:17:15.690 --> 00:17:18.000
However, you should be careful.

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.720
We only get one life.

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:24.380
If you keep up this nonsense, 
I'll call the cops!

00:17:24.380 --> 00:17:26.270
Go ahead and call them.

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:31.190
A place shrouded in a miasma this thick 
might need the rescue squad.

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:36.650
Why would you stain them with such ugliness?

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:41.830
Misused gemstones bring misfortune.

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:46.180
I wholeheartedly recommend 
that you all find better employment

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:49.710
and get yourselves exorcised 
at the appropriate places.

00:17:56.960 --> 00:18:00.050
Now, everyone, do take care.

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:05.680
Bending an ear to the 
murmur of these gemstones

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:09.190
is all I can do for you.

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:23.870
Get the salt!

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:31.540
I apologize for involving you
 in something so dangerous.

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:34.170
I knew what I was getting into.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:36.760
Anyway, are you okay?

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:38.800
They know who you are now.

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:44.790
This business isn't as 
clean as you think it is.

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:49.120
Is that why you used the name Edward Baxter?

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:56.190
When I heard you were going, 
I was determined to go with you.

00:18:57.340 --> 00:18:58.570
Do you know why?

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:00.860
Because you're a hero of justice?

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:02.620
Because I was worried!

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:05.440
You were being reckless for once.

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:11.460
Do you have some kind of history 
with turquoise fraud or something?

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:12.690
No.

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:18.720
I simply abhor those who use the 
power of gemstones for selfish desires.

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:22.720
It goes without saying that I feel similarly 
about con artists who prey on others.

00:19:23.940 --> 00:19:25.690
Is that really all?

00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:34.960
Men who use their looks to 
sell counterfeit gemstones

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:36.650
make me want to vomit.

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:40.400
On top of that, his pick-up line
 is, "It's real"? Laughable.

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:55.920
Happy Étoile is a scam! 
#pleaserepost #faketurquoise

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:55.920
Richard

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:55.920
You have a new message.

00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:55.920
Richard?

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:00.650
<i>My colleague contacted me.</i>

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:04.050
<i>Happy Étoile disappeared overnight.</i>

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:08.990
You're way more of a hero 
of justice than I am.

00:20:23.770 --> 00:20:26.190
Edward Baxter.

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:30.250
Who are you?

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:34.240
You're the Caucasian jeweler who's been

00:20:34.240 --> 00:20:37.750
scamming tourists for the 
past month, aren't you?

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:43.630
That's the gemstone I sold yesterday.
What's going on?

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:47.210
It seems the German couple you sold this to

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:50.810
bought it thinking it was a topaz,

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:53.890
but no. This is a blue zircon.

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:59.110
What's wrong with selling the more expensive 
blue zircon at the price of a topaz?

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:03.270
Lying in order to sell a customer 
something they don't want

00:21:03.270 --> 00:21:06.590
isn't something a jeweler should do.

00:21:07.090 --> 00:21:09.970
Gemstone scams are an everyday occurrence.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:17.710
Is your real name Richard?

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:21.250
You sell fake gemstones and use a fake name.

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:22.710
Bad for you.

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:25.770
You diminish yourself.

00:21:26.480 --> 00:21:30.350
That said, there's some value 
in your conversational skills.

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:34.200
That German couple was quite happy.

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:39.480
Even without those looks of yours, 
there's still something to you.

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:42.480
Don't talk about my face. It offends me.

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:48.880
I see. So that's your strongest asset.

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:51.050
I apologize for the slip of the tongue.

00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:54.920
I am Saul Ranashinha.

00:21:54.920 --> 00:21:57.010
I have a proposal for you.
